{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And YHWH spoke to Moses after the death of the two sons of Aaron, etc.</b> What does this teach? Rabbi Elazar ben Azaryah would compare it to a parable of a sick person into whom a physician entered. He said to him: Do not eat cold food and do not sleep in a damp place. Another came and said to him: Do not eat cold food and do not sleep in a damp place, lest you die in the manner that so-and-so died — this one spurred him on more than the first. Therefore it says: 'after the death of the two sons of Aaron.'"], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:06:40.529410798Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}